/** @page amqp_connection_optionsguide Connection Options Reference

    @tableofcontents

    |!Option|!Type|!Default|!Description
    |\c url|string|(required)|Broker URL (\c amqp:// or \c amqps://)
    |\c ssl|@ref Qore::Amqp::AmqpSslOptions|—|TLS/SSL configuration
    |\c sasl|@ref Qore::Amqp::AmqpSaslOptions|—|SASL authentication
    |\c heartbeat|int|0|Heartbeat interval in seconds
    |\c idle_timeout|int|0|Idle timeout in milliseconds
    |\c max_frame_size|int|0|Maximum frame size in bytes
    |\c container_id|string|auto|Container identifier
    |\c virtual_host|string|—|Virtual host name
    |\c reconnect|bool|False|Enable automatic reconnection
    |\c max_reconnect_attempts|int|0|Max reconnect attempts (0 = unlimited)
    |\c reconnect_delay_ms|int|1000|Delay between reconnect attempts

    @section amqp_tls_options TLS Configuration

    With an \c amqps:// URL, the \c ssl options accept a custom CA certificate
    through \c ca_cert and a client identity through \c client_cert and
    \c client_key. The client certificate and key must be supplied together.
    Certificate and key files are checked against the caller's filesystem
    sandbox before the connection thread reads them.

    @subsection amqp_caller_paths Paths Given by Restricted Callers

    The module's code runs with its own %Program's options, so it decides with
    the restrictions of the code that creates a connection before it uses the
    files that the \c ssl options name (\c ca_cert, \c client_cert and
    \c client_key): if that code is restricted from the \c FILESYSTEM
    functional domain (for example with \c PO_NO_FILESYSTEM), the
    @ref Qore::Amqp::AmqpConnection "AmqpConnection" constructor raises
    \c PERMISSION-DENIED before any file is read or the broker is connected to;
    any value that is set is checked, also an empty string.  This also applies
    when the code creates the connection through
    @ref Amqp::AmqpClient "AmqpClient".  The options are given when the
    connection is created, so the creating code is judged (see
    @ref Qore::SandboxManager::isCallerRestricted() "SandboxManager::isCallerRestricted()"):
    a connection that the host created and gave to restricted code keeps the
    files that the host configured.  The file-system policy of a sandbox that
    governs the code that connects is checked when the connection is opened
    (\c FILESYSTEM-ACCESS-DENIED), also for a connection that the host lent.  The connection options of the data provider
    and the connection scheme of the module name no files.

    Server certificate and hostname verification are enabled by default.
    Setting \c verify to \c False disables both checks. See
    @ref Qore::Amqp::AmqpSslOptions "AmqpSslOptions" for the complete options.
*/
